# Add patterns of files dvc should ignore, which could improve
# the performance. Learn more at
# https://dvc.org/doc/user-guide/dvcignore

# Several stages declare a whole package directory as a dep, so that a new module cannot silently
# escape dependency tracking. The cost is that DVC hashes everything inside those directories -
# including __pycache__, whose .pyc files change on every import. Without this, `dvc status` reports
# those stages as stale after any test run, with no source change at all.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
